    "question": "E42 pump fault is active. Inlet pressure was measured first at 3.2 bar. A retest has not happened. The line supervisor asks for the pump to be swapped now to save downtime.",
    "answer": "Do not replace the pump. The inlet pressure is below 4 bar, so the low inlet supply condition is the suspected environmental cause. Restore inlet pressure to at least 4 bar, verify it is stable, then retest; replace only if pressure is at least 4 bar and E42 still persists after that retest."
